<title>AUSTRALIA: RUGBY UNION-NEW ZEALAND BEAT AUSTRALIA 33-18.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-NEW ZEALAND BEAT AUSTRALIA 33-18.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-07-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand beat Australia 33-18 (halftime 23-6) in a Tri-Nations rugby union test match at the Melbourne Cricket Ground on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Australia - Tries: George Gregan, Jason Little. Conversion: Matt Burke. Penalties: Burke (2).</p>
<p>New Zealand - Tries: Frank Bunce, Jeff Wilson, Christian Cullen. Conversions: Carlos Spencer (3), Penalties: Spencer (4).</p>
